@startuml Attack Enemy - Communication Diagram
!theme plain
title **UC-2: Attack Enemy – Communication Diagram**

object ":GameView" as ui #LightBlue
object ":GameController" as ctrl #LightGreen
object ":CombatEngine" as combat #Salmon
object ":AttackAction" as aa #LightYellow
object ":DamageEffect" as de #Orange
object ":Hero" as hero #Pink
object ":Enemy" as enemy #Red
object ":GameSession" as sess #White

ui -- ctrl
ctrl -- combat
ctrl -- aa
ctrl -- de
ctrl -- sess
combat -- aa
aa -- hero
aa -- enemy
aa -- de
de -- enemy

ui -> ctrl : 1: executeAction(attackAction)
ctrl -> combat : 1.1: performAttack(hero, enemy)
combat -> aa : 1.1.1: <<create>> AttackAction(hero, enemy)
combat -> ctrl : 1.1.2: executeAction(attackAction)
ctrl -> aa : 1.1.2.1: resolve(session)
aa -> hero : 1.1.2.1.1: isAlive()
aa -> enemy : 1.1.2.1.2: isAlive()
aa -> hero : 1.1.2.1.3: calculateDamage()
aa -> de : 1.1.2.1.4: <<create>> DamageEffect(enemy, damage)
ctrl -> de : 1.1.2.2: apply(session)
de -> enemy : 1.1.2.2.1: takeDamage(damage)
ctrl -> sess : 1.1.2.3: advanceTurn()

note bottom of ctrl
  **GRASP Controller**: GameController orchestrates.
  **Creator**: CombatEngine creates AttackAction
  (it has initializing data: attacker & defender).
  **Information Expert**: Hero.calculateDamage()
  includes weapon bonus.
end note

@enduml
